<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Emirate of Cyrenaica</h1><p class="st-meta">1949 CE – 1951 CE · capital Benghazi</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived emirate proclaimed by Idris al-Senussi with British backing in 1949, the stepping stone to an independent united Libya.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Idris, head of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/senussi-order">Senussi Order</a>, had allied with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>. On 1 June 1949, with British approval, he proclaimed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrenaica">Cyrenaica</a> independent at Benghazi under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/british-military-administration-of-libya">British Military Administration of Libya</a>, as the UN debated the future of the former Italian colony.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> had its own government and a constitution of 1949, with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> retaining control of foreign affairs and defence. It was based on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bedouin">Bedouin</a> tribes loyal to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/senussi-order">Senussi</a>, and Benghazi served as its capital.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Idris negotiated union with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tripolitania">Tripolitania</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sultanate-of-fezzan">Fezzan</a>, and on 24 December 1951 he became king of the federal <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-libya">Kingdom of Libya</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrenaica">Cyrenaica</a> as one of its provinces.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/emirate-of-cyrenaica.jpg" alt="Emirate of Cyrenaica" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: An Encore Performance From The Boys In The Band · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Cyrenaica.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1949 CE – 1951 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Benghazi</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Idris al-Senussi</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam (Senussi)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/libya">Libya</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Cyrenaica Emirate</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1950&amp;focus=emirate-of-cyrenaica" aria-label="Emirate of Cyrenaica on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5196 1009 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Emirate of Cyrenaica lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5516 1265L5638 1347M5516 1265L4997 651M5516 1265L5338 1239"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5638 1347h0M4997 651h0M5338 1239h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5516 1265h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5516 1265h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Benghazi. <a href="/atlas?year=1950&amp;focus=emirate-of-cyrenaica">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
